<div class="container my-5">
  <h2 class="text-center text-primary mb-4">About Telugu Community Hamburg e.V.</h2>

  <p class="lead text-justify">
    <strong>Telugu Community Hamburg (TCH) e.V.</strong> is a registered, non-profit organization (VR 25642) that has been serving the Telugu and Indian communities in Hamburg and across Germany for over 15 years. Our mission is rooted in preserving and promoting the rich heritage of Telugu culture, language, and Sanatana Dharma while building an inclusive and integrated society abroad.
  </p>

  <h4 class="text-danger-emphasis mt-4 alert alert-info">Our Mission</h4>
  <p class="text-justify">
    Our mission is to <strong>Preserve, Promote, and Pass on</strong> the Telugu culture and values to future generations, while also building a spiritually enriching environment for all. We aim to integrate communities, foster inclusiveness, and inspire the next generation to stay connected with their roots—socially, culturally, and spiritually.
  </p>

  <h4 class="text-danger-emphasis alert alert-info mt-4">Our Journey & Milestones</h4>
  <p class="text-justify">
    What started in 2016 as a humble volunteer group has grown into a dynamic and trusted organization in Hamburg. TCH e.V. has organized historic events such as:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
    <li class="list-group-item">🌸 First-ever <strong>TTD Sri Srinivasa Kalyanams</strong> in Germany (2023 & 2024)</li>
    <li class="list-group-item">🌺 First-ever <strong>Sita Rama Kalyanam</strong> in Germany (2024)</li>
    <li class="list-group-item">🕉️ Regular <strong>weekly poojas</strong> and spiritual gatherings at Sri Hindu Mandir, Hamburg</li>
    <li class="list-group-item">📜 Language classes and cultural workshops for children (ages 5–16)</li>
    <li class="list-group-item">💼 Hosting <strong>international summits</strong> and AP state visits in Hamburg</li>
    <li class="list-group-item">🤝 Emergency aid and social services for NRI families in distress</li>
  </ul>

  <h4 class="text-danger-emphasis alert alert-info mt-4">How We Serve the Community</h4>
  <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
    <li class="list-group-item">
      🎭 <strong>Cultural Events:</strong> Organizing Ugadi, Dasara Bathukamma, Deepavali, and other festivals to foster cross-cultural celebration and pride in our heritage.
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
      📚 <strong>Language & Education:</strong> Telugu and Sanskrit classes, youth workshops, and public education to instill language pride and knowledge.
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
      🛠️ <strong>Integration Support:</strong> Help with German language learning, job searches, and accommodation for newcomers.
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
      🧘‍♀️ <strong>Wellness & Yoga:</strong> Organizing yoga sessions for physical and mental well-being, open to all communities.
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
      🧡 <strong>Emergency Services:</strong> Providing financial and emotional support to families affected by tragedies, including fire victims and flood relief.
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
      👩‍🦰 <strong>Women Empowerment:</strong> “Voice of Woman (VoW)” initiative to encourage leadership and growth among women in our community.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h4 class="text-danger-emphasis alert alert-info mt-4">Our Temple Vision</h4>
  <p class="text-justify">
    In 2024, the divine murthys of Sri Srinivasa, Sridevi, and Bhoodevi were brought to Hamburg and placed for public darshan. Weekly poojas have since become a spiritual anchor for our community. TCH e.V. is actively working with TTD and local authorities toward the construction of a <strong>permanent Sri Balaji Temple in Hamburg</strong>—a historic milestone in our spiritual journey.
  </p>

  <h4 class="text-danger-emphasis alert alert-info mt-4">Leadership & Collaboration</h4>
  <p class="text-justify">
    TCH e.V. maintains strong ties with the Indian Consulate, Government of Andhra Pradesh, APNRT, and TTD. Our president, Sri Rajendra Prasad, has proudly served as the APNRT Coordinator for Germany for over 9 years, fostering cross-border collaboration and community unity.
  </p>

  <h4 class="text-danger-emphasis alert alert-info mt-4">Join Us</h4>
  <p class="text-justify">
    Telugu Community Hamburg e.V. welcomes everyone—Telugu-speaking or otherwise—who shares our values of unity, inclusivity, and cultural pride. Be a part of our journey as we work together to preserve our dharma and uplift our community in Germany and beyond.
  </p>
</div>
